A host runs many conversations in one process, each with credentials of
its own, and holds none itself. pi reads a configured key, checks a
provider is set up before a prompt, and lists available models through
an auth context that defaults to the process's environment, and
ModelRuntime offers no way to give it another. A hosted conversation
therefore found no key, or would have found the host's.

Let ModelRuntime.create take an auth context and hand it to the models
it builds, and mark the build so a host can refuse one without it.
Resolve a configured key only when the context holds it, as the check
before a prompt already does, so a key the context lacks never comes
from the process. Without a context, pi reads the process as before.

Offered upstream as the model auth-context host seam. Apply only to the
host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays unchanged.

